//File:    recipes.local.jtext.example
//Date:    2026-10-30
//Purpose: Example of a machine-local override of recipes.jtext (v002). Copy it to
//         Setup/recipes.local.jtext (gitignored, never committed) and edit; this .example file is
//         never read. jac313_test_cli (settings.cpp) and bsir.sh (Setup/jtext_table.sh) read
//         recipes.jtext with the local file's rows applied, row by row:
//
//   - The local file has both sections of recipes.jtext (components, recipe_os), each with every
//     column of the tracked one (a section may have no rows), plus an optional Bool column
//     delete. A column the tracked table does not have is an error.
//   - A row's key: components: component; recipe_os: os + component.
//   - A row whose key recipes.jtext has REPLACES that row (in place, every column); a new key is
//     ADDED after the tracked rows; a row with delete = true REMOVES the row with its key (the
//     other columns of that row are not used; nothing happens when no row has the key). Rows
//     apply in file order. id is not part of the key.
//   - No local file = recipes.jtext as it is. A local file that does not read or validate, or
//     lacks a section or a column, is an error naming it (the CLI stops; bsir.sh says so and
//     stops). `jac313_test_cli setup` prints "local overrides: <file> (N rows)".
//
// This example: Fedora installs ninja from its own package (override), a tmux component with its
// Fedora command (add), and no DBeaver on this machine (remove).
//
// Same formatter as recipes.jtext (^~), one row per line, no comments on data rows: bsir.sh reads
// this file with POSIX awk.
//
=== jText File ===
 1. ?# recipes.local.jtext
 2. ?# 2026-10-30
 3. ?# Machine-local provision recipe overrides (v002)
 4. ?# 0.8

=== Section: components ===
=== Fields ===
 1. /# id/Integer/Not Null
 2. /# component/String/Not Null/Not Empty
 3. /# desc/String/Not Null/Not Empty
 4. /# for/String/Not Null
 5. /# required/Bool/Not Null
 6. /# check/String/Not Null
 7. /# delete/Bool/Not Null                      # true = remove the tracked row with this key
=== End Fields ===
=== Data ===
 1. ^~ 1^tmux^tmux (terminal multiplexer)^^false^command -v tmux >/dev/null 2>&1^false
 1. ^~ 2^dbeaver^-^^false^^true
=== End Data ===
=== End Section ===

=== Section: recipe_os ===
=== Fields ===
 1. /# id/Integer/Not Null
 2. /# os/String/Not Null/Not Empty
 3. /# component/String/Not Null/Not Empty
 4. /# command/String/Not Null/Not Empty
 5. /# delete/Bool/Not Null                      # true = remove the tracked row with this key
=== End Fields ===
=== Data ===
 1. ^~ 1^fedora^ninja^sudo dnf install -y ninja-build^false
 1. ^~ 2^fedora^tmux^sudo dnf install -y tmux^false
=== End Data ===
=== End Section ===
=== End File ===
